module prelude
edition 0


note: The 21 prelude functions written in Sayform (spec/12-stdlib.md section 3). The constant empty-set is provided by the host because no Sayform expression builds an empty set.
a Pair of A and B has a left (A) and a right (B)


to less-eq x y giving a truth:
    give back not y is less than x


to greater x y giving a truth:
    give back y is less than x


to greater-eq x y giving a truth:
    give back not x is less than y


to between x lo hi with low-inclusive (a truth, default yes) with high-inclusive (a truth, default yes) giving a truth:
    let above be lo is less than x or (low-inclusive and lo equals x)
    give back above and (x is less than hi or (high-inclusive and x equals hi))


to absolute of x (a number) giving a number:
    if x is less than 0:
        give back negative x
    give back x


to checked-divide x (a number) by d (a number) giving a number, may fail with division-by-zero:
    if d equals 0:
        give back problem division-by-zero with message "cannot divide by zero"
    give back x divided by d


to join-all of items (a list of text) by sep (text) giving text:
    let out be "", changeable
    let first-item be yes, changeable
    for each piece in items:
        if first-item:
            set out to out joined with piece
            set first-item to no
        otherwise:
            set out to out joined with sep joined with piece
    give back out


to map of c f giving anything:
    if c is a map from anything to anything:
        let out be {}, changeable
        for each k in keys of c:
            add {k: f(item k of c)} to out
        give back out
    let out be [], changeable
    if c is a set of anything:
        set out to empty-set
    for each x in c:
        add f(x) to out
    give back out


to filter of c f giving anything:
    let out be [], changeable
    if c is a set of anything:
        set out to empty-set
    for each x in c:
        if f(x):
            add x to out
    give back out


to sort of c giving a list of anything:
    give back sort-by(c, given x, x)


to first of c giving anything or nothing:
    give back item 1 of c, if any


to last of c giving anything or nothing:
    give back item negative 1 of c, if any


to take n (an integer) from c giving a list of anything:
    let out be [], changeable
    for each x in c:
        if count of out equals n:
            stop
        add x to out
    give back out


to drop n (an integer) from c giving a list of anything:
    let out be [], changeable
    let seen be 0, changeable
    for each x in c:
        if seen is at least n:
            add x to out
        add 1 to seen
    give back out


to sum of c giving a number:
    let total be 0, changeable
    for each x in c:
        set total to total plus x
    give back total


to group-by of c key giving a map from anything to lists of anything:
    let groups be {}, changeable
    for each x in c:
        let k be key(x)
        let existing be item k of groups, if any
        add {k: added(existing or else [], x)} to groups
    give back groups


to zip xs (a list of A) ys (a list of B) giving a list of pairs, for any A and B:
    let out be [], changeable
    let i be 1, changeable
    while (i is at most count of xs) and i is at most count of ys:
        add (Pair with left (item i of xs) and right item i of ys) to out
        add 1 to i
    give back out


to is-empty of c giving a truth:
    give back count of c equals 0


to reversed of c (a list of anything) giving a list of anything:
    let out be [], changeable
    for each x in c:
        set out to [x] joined with out
    give back out


to largest of items (a list of T) giving a T or nothing, for any T:
    give back last of sort of items


to smallest of items (a list of T) giving a T or nothing, for any T:
    give back first of sort of items
